  "boundary": [
    "Strict decode verifies one session and exact selected class names. It returns observed IDs and probe data; no expected physical CRC is passed into this decoder.",
    "UnfilteredCodeMeasurement requires at least one explicit .class. It computes CRC on the bytes, reads the internal name from those bytes, rejects same-name/wrong-CRC and same-CRC/wrong-name, and separately checks probe layout. Its class records can report missing execution.",
    "The PG39868 caller freezes the nonempty nine-path list from a defined scope, checks compiled hashes and measurement names, requires true command completion before processing rows, and compares positive IDs with saved same-run session/class output. Negative/no-Code rows keep their own status.",
    "The known empty-set consumer uses the reader output for session only and checks a separate physical metadata inventory. Zero requested class results carries zero class qualification.",
    "PG40268 independently supplies two Java25 class files and CRC from their bytes. Late second-class mismatch emits one good first row, then exit 1. The strict reader alone reports both named records, so accepting a name match or partial rows would miss physical failure.",
    "451 requires a source/run-bound aggregate and full independent current qualification. The provided receipts do not include same-current-source owned native capture, complete class/CRC, owner/session and terminal proof."
  ],
